<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">💡</span><div class="callout__content">
<p><strong>Self-study quiz.</strong> This quiz is for your own review — answers are not recorded. You’ll get instant feedback on each question.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="quiz"><div class="quiz__top-bar"><div class="quiz__score-tracker" style="display:none;"></div><button class="quiz__start-over" type="button" style="display:none;">Start Over</button></div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q1c">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">1</span> What is the medium of dance?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1a" id="q1a">
        <label for="q1a">Words and sentences only.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1b" id="q1b">
        <label for="q1b">Stone and bronze.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1c" id="q1c">
        <label for="q1c">The human body and motion.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1d" id="q1d">
        <label for="q1d">Paint and canvas.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Dance uses the body as its medium and movement as its material.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Dance has no external material. The body itself is the medium, and motion is what it works with.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q2b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">2</span> The lesson says that dance's subject matter can be</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2a" id="q2a">
        <label for="q2a">only the music being played.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2b" id="q2b">
        <label for="q2b">abstract (pure movement and pattern), emotional (feelings expressed through gesture), or narrative (a story told through choreography).</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2c" id="q2c">
        <label for="q2c">only historical events.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2d" id="q2d">
        <label for="q2d">only religious stories.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The lesson stresses that feeling is dance's most fundamental subject matter, because the body communicates emotional states more directly than words.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Think of the three kinds of dance in the lesson: pure pattern, expressed feeling, and told story.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q3b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">3</span> How did modern dance differ from ballet?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3a" id="q3a">
        <label for="q3a">It required pointe shoes.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3b" id="q3b">
        <label for="q3b">It rejected ballet's formalized movements in favor of natural, expressive motion rooted in breath, weight, and the floor.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3c" id="q3c">
        <label for="q3c">It used a larger codified vocabulary.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3d" id="q3d">
        <label for="q3d">It was always performed without a body.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Pioneers such as Isadora Duncan and Martha Graham wanted movement that came from the body's own impulses.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Modern dance was a reaction against ballet's fixed vocabulary. Look for the answer about natural, expressive motion.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q4a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">4</span> What is the earliest root of dance named in the lesson?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4a" id="q4a">
        <label for="q4a">Ritual: ceremonial dances such as rain dances and harvest dances.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4b" id="q4b">
        <label for="q4b">Film.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4c" id="q4c">
        <label for="q4c">Television.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4d" id="q4d">
        <label for="q4d">Photography.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The path runs from ritual through court dance and ballet to modern and contemporary forms.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Dance is far older than any of the media in the other options. The lesson traces it to ceremonial dances.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q5d">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">5</span> In Martha Graham's Lamentation, what does the fabric do?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5a" id="q5a">
        <label for="q5a">It tells a detailed story of a specific event.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5b" id="q5b">
        <label for="q5b">It hides the dancer so she cannot be seen.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5c" id="q5c">
        <label for="q5c">It is a costume only for decoration.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5d" id="q5d">
        <label for="q5d">It acts as a second skin that both contains and reveals the body's anguish, as the dancer presses it into angular shapes.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Graham said she was not depicting sorrow but showing what sorrow does to the body.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The fabric is part of the dance's form. It stretches into shapes that show grief without illustrating a particular event.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q6d">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">6</span> Which sequence describes the three sections of Alvin Ailey's Revelations?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6a" id="q6a">
        <label for="q6a">Birth, marriage, and death.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6b" id="q6b">
        <label for="q6b">Past, present, and future.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6c" id="q6c">
        <label for="q6c">Spring, summer, and autumn.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6d" id="q6d">
        <label for="q6d">Struggle (Pilgrim of Sorrow), baptism and purification (Take Me to the Water), and celebration (Move, Members, Move).</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The dance moves from earthbound, weighted movement to soaring, joyful lifts, and it grows from the rhythms and emotions of spirituals.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Revelations follows an emotional arc that begins in struggle and ends in joy, with a ritual of baptism in between.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q7a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">7</span> Why does the repetition of falls and catches in Pina Bausch's Café Müller matter?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7a" id="q7a">
        <label for="q7a">It builds an emotional content about the difficulty of human connection and the compulsion to keep reaching for it.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7b" id="q7b">
        <label for="q7b">It is only a way to fill time.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7c" id="q7c">
        <label for="q7c">It always becomes boring.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7d" id="q7d">
        <label for="q7d">It shows the dancers need more practice.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Repetition is one of the most important structural features of dance form; it can intensify instead of weaken.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The lesson treats repetition as structure. Here it builds a feeling about people who keep reaching for contact despite repeated failure.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q8b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">8</span> In the four questions for looking at dance, level (high, middle, low) and direction belong to which question?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8a" id="q8a">
        <label for="q8a">Time.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8b" id="q8b">
        <label for="q8b">Space.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8c" id="q8c">
        <label for="q8c">Body.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8d" id="q8d">
        <label for="q8d">Energy.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Space covers where dancers go, direction, level, and the distances between them.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Space concerns where the dancers go on the stage and how they use direction and level.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q9a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">9</span> Which kinds of dance does the lesson count as part of the art form's living tradition?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9a" id="q9a">
        <label for="q9a">Popular forms such as hip-hop, tap, jookin, and ballroom.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9b" id="q9b">
        <label for="q9b">Only ballet.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9c" id="q9c">
        <label for="q9c">Only dances without music.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9d" id="q9d">
        <label for="q9d">Only ritual dances of the distant past.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Contemporary choreographers also blend traditions, such as ballet technique with street-dance vocabulary.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The lesson says popular dance forms are part of dance's living tradition, not outside it.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q10c">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">10</span> What does Gene Kelly's dance in Singin' in the Rain show about the elements of dance?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10a" id="q10a">
        <label for="q10a">That dance needs no body.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10b" id="q10b">
        <label for="q10b">That dance must be silent.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10c" id="q10c">
        <label for="q10c">Tap steps, an umbrella, and puddles can express joy through body, space, time, and energy.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10d" id="q10d">
        <label for="q10d">That dance cannot be filmed.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The movement's bounce and playfulness is the content. A rainy street becomes a place of joy through form.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Look at what the dancer does with the umbrella and puddles. The joy is expressed through the quality of the movement.</div>
  </div>
</div>

